@BookSearchService_HostAddress = http://localhost:5014

### Specific work — exercises title + author dedicated params
GET {{BookSearchService_HostAddress}}/api/books/search?q=dune by frank herbert
Accept: application/json

### Vague query — returns 0 results and times out if sent raw to OpenLibrary.
### Getting real books back here is the proof that parsing before retrieval works.
GET {{BookSearchService_HostAddress}}/api/books/search?q=gritty space opera about corporate politics
Accept: application/json

### Confirms keywords became subject: filters rather than free text
GET {{BookSearchService_HostAddress}}/api/books/search?q=cyberpunk dystopian novels
Accept: application/json

### Year range — should parse into first_publish_year:[1990 TO 1999]
GET {{BookSearchService_HostAddress}}/api/books/search?q=cyberpunk novels from the 90s
Accept: application/json

### Cache check, part 1 — expect a slow response (AI call + catalog round trip)
GET {{BookSearchService_HostAddress}}/api/books/search?q=books by stephen king
Accept: application/json

### Cache check, part 2 — different wording, same meaning.
### Must be a cache hit: fast, and no Gemini/OpenLibrary lines in the log.
GET {{BookSearchService_HostAddress}}/api/books/search?q=KING, Stephen books!
Accept: application/json

### Validation — empty q returns 400 ProblemDetails
GET {{BookSearchService_HostAddress}}/api/books/search?q=
Accept: application/json
